# Multi-Tenant Database Isolation Rules

## 1. Mandatory Multi-Tenancy Discriminators
- Every single entity schema interacting with multi-vendor structures must map a strict foreign key relationship to `vendor_id` or `store_id`.
- Global platform tracking systems are the only exclusion allowed from this rule.

## 2. PostgreSQL Row-Level Security (RLS) Compliance
- All database read/write queries generated via MikroORM repository adapters must execute through a proxy session tracking the transaction context client identity configuration parameters.
- Read current tenant data models context asynchronously using `AsyncLocalStorage` initialized at the incoming request execution boundary.
- Do not write raw SQL bypass queries that omit the dynamic tenant connection parameter checks.

## 3. Performance & Schema Constraints
- Dynamic product configurations and unpredictable structural item variants must be mapped explicitly within highly flexible PostgreSQL `JSONB` parameters.
- Provide custom index configurations (`GIN` indexes) across high-frequency lookup fields mapped within JSON structures.
- All monetary attributes must be stored as integers representing fractions/Paisa to prevent floating-point calculation drift.
